      "id": "lq_1",
      "question": "What is the difference between a hard link and a soft link?",
      "answer": "A hard link points directly to the same inode as the original file — deleting the original doesn't break it, and\nboth share the same data on disk. A soft (symbolic) link is a pointer to the file path; if the original is deleted or\nmoved, the symlink breaks. Hard links can't cross filesystems or link to directories; symlinks can.",
      "level": "junior",
      "source": "100 DevOps Master Q&A",
