      "question": "What's the difference between a process and a thread?",
      "answer": "A process is an independent execution unit with its own memory space; threads are lightweight units within a\nprocess that share the same memory space but have their own stack. Threads are cheaper to create and\ncommunicate faster, but a crash in one can affect the whole process.",
