      "id": "lq_7",
      "question": "Explain the difference between TCP and UDP.",
      "answer": "TCP is connection-oriented, guarantees ordered and reliable delivery via handshakes and acknowledgments —\nused for HTTP, SSH, databases. UDP is connectionless, faster, with no delivery guarantee — used for DNS,\nvideo streaming, and cases where speed matters more than reliability.",
