      "id": "lq_8",
      "question": "What is a zombie process and how do you handle it?",
      "answer": "A zombie is a process that has completed execution but still has an entry in the process table because its parent\nhasn't read its exit status. It doesn't consume resources itself; you fix it by getting the parent process to call\nwait(), or by killing the parent if it's misbehaving.\n2. Git & Version Control",
