      "question": "How do you implement Ephemeral PR Preview Environments in a Kubernetes CI/CD pipeline?",
      "answer": "1. On GitHub PR open/update event, CI workflow triggers.<br>2. Builds container image tagged with PR commit SHA.<br>3. Creates a dedicated dynamic namespace: <code>pr-123</code> in non-prod cluster.<br>4. Deploys application with Helm/Kustomize, configuring dynamic Ingress host: <code>pr-123.preview.company.com</code>.<br>5. Posts automated preview URL comment on the GitHub PR.<br>6. On PR merge/close event, cleanup workflow triggers: <code>kubectl delete ns pr-123</code> to reclaim resources.",
