      "question": "Docker & Container Engineering #14: Explain the production best practice for managing host bind mounts vs named volumes performance.",
      "answer": "This is a fundamental interview question evaluating your understanding of architectural tradeoffs.\n\n- **Primary Difference:** The two concepts serve distinct purposes in modern infrastructure design, balancing speed, consistency, and operational complexity.\n- **Key Characteristics:** One approach prioritizes declarative state and immutability, while the other offers flexibility for dynamic runtime environments.\n- **When to Use Each:** Choose based on workload requirements, high-availability guarantees, and rollback complexity in production.\n\n*Pro Tip:* In interviews, always structure your answer by stating the high-level definition first, followed by 2-3 specific technical comparison points and a real-world production example.",
