      "id": "k100_4",
      "question": "What is the relationship between Kubernetes and Docker?",
      "answer": "o Answer: Docker is a containerization platform that enables you to\npackage and run applications in isolated environments called containers.\nKubernetes is a container orchestration platform that manages and\nautomates the deployment, scaling, and operation of Docker containers\n(or any other OCI-compliant container runtime) across a cluster of\nmachines. Docker builds the house (container), Kubernetes manages the\nneighborhood (cluster).",
      "level": "junior",
      "source": "100 Kubernetes Interview Questions",
      "tags": [
        "Kubernetes",
        "K8s",
        "CloudNative"
      ]
