      "id": "k100_53",
      "question": "What is the Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF)?",
      "answer": "**What is the Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF)** is a key component in modern cloud-native engineering.\n\n- **Core Function:** It provides standardized, reliable mechanisms to manage state, orchestrate workloads, or enforce infrastructure consistency.\n- **Production Value:** Eliminates manual operational overhead, ensures high availability, and facilitates automated recovery during system failures.\n- **Best Practice:** Ensure proper observability, automated linting/validation, and version control are integrated into the lifecycle of this component.\n\n*Pro Tip:* Frame your response around the problem this technology solves and how it improves system reliability and developer velocity.",
